{
  "index": 11,
  "text": "This single-arm, multicenter, prospective phase II clinical study was conducted at 4 medical centers across China. The clinical trial was registered at ClinicalTrials.gov under the identifier NCT05348668. Eligible patients (18 to 75 years) had histologically confirmed stage IV driver-negative NSCLC (8th edition of the Tumor\u2013Node\u2013Metastasis [TNM] Staging System 24), Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status 0 to 1, and adequate organ/bone marrow function. Exclusion criteria included driver mutations (e.g., epidermal growth factor receptor [EGFR], anaplastic lymphoma kinase [ALK], and ROS proto-oncogene 1 [ROS1]), pulmonary fibrosis, autoimmune disease, active infection, or serious comorbidities. All patients received 4 to 6 cycles of platinum-based doublet chemotherapy plus ICI. Patients without disease progression after comprehensive evaluation subsequently underwent Hybrid-RT during ICI maintenance. The comprehensive clinical trial protocol is provided in Data S1.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 14,
  "text": "Eligibility to participate in the study required histologically confirmed diagnosis and completion of molecular profiling (including at least EGFR, ALK, ROS1, and programmed cell death ligand 1 [PD-L1] status). All patients were pre-evaluated and staged via bronchoscopy, computed tomography (CT) with contrast, contrast-enhanced magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the brain, and single-photon emission CT bone scan; positron emission tomography (PET)/CT or PET/MRI was optional. Histopathological diagnosis of suspicious lymph nodes was established via either thoracoscopic biopsy or endosonography-guided needle aspiration as clinically warranted.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 16,
  "text": "All enrolled patients received 4 to 6 cycles of standard platinum-based doublet chemotherapy combined with ICI therapy. Specific chemotherapy regimens and ICI agents were selected at the investigators\u2019 discretion in accordance with both the National Comprehensive Cancer Network guidelines 25 and the Chinese Society of Clinical Oncology guidelines. ICI maintenance continued for up to 24 months or until disease progression, unacceptable toxicity, or study withdrawal occurred.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 18,
  "text": "Patients without progression after chemoimmunotherapy received Hybrid-RT during ICI maintenance, completed within 3 months. SABR-eligible lesions were treated with hypofractionated radiotherapy (24 Gy/3 fractions or 50 Gy/4 to 5 fractions), while non-SABR lesions received LDRT (6 to 15 Gy at 1.5 Gy/fraction). For patients who were restaged as stage III disease after chemoimmunotherapy, the primary tumor and regional metastatic lymph nodes received short-course hypofractionated radiotherapy with 48 Gy in 12 fractions, which achieves a biologically effective dose (BED) equivalent to conventional fractionation of 54 Gy in 27 fractions (assuming an \u03b1/\u03b2 ratio of 10 Gy for NSCLC). Target selection and dose schedules are detailed in Tables S1 and S2. The simulation utilized customized vacuum immobilization with intravenous contrast-enhanced 4-dimensional CT. The internal target volume (ITV) was contoured on maximum intensity projection reconstructions, with the planning target volume defined as the ITV plus a 5-mm isotropic margin. All treatments followed predefined plans, minimizing inter-/intra-fractional errors.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 20,
  "text": "The primary endpoint was the 1-year progression-free survival (PFS) rate. PFS was defined as the time from initiation of first-line chemoimmunotherapy to disease progression per Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST v1.1) or death from any cause, whichever occurred first. Patients without documented disease progression or death at the time of data cutoff were censored at the date of their last disease assessment. The secondary endpoints were median PFS, 1.5-year and 2-year PFS rates, median overall survival (OS), 1-year and 2-year OS rates, objective response rate (ORR), disease control rate (DCR), and adverse events (AEs). OS was defined as the time from initiation of first-line chemoimmunotherapy to death from any cause (living patients were censored at last follow-up). Per RECIST v1.1, ORR and DCR represented patients achieving complete or partial response, and complete/partial response or stable disease, respectively. Hybrid-RT was initiated no less than 2 weeks after the completion of initial chemoimmunotherapy. Exploratory outcomes included changes in peripheral blood lymphocyte subsets pre-radiotherapy and 3 weeks post-radiotherapy. AEs and laboratory/radiological assessments were performed weekly during chemoimmunotherapy and radiotherapy, and every 3 weeks during ICI maintenance. AEs were graded according to the Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events (CTCAE version 4.0). Tumor assessments per RECIST v1.1 were conduct

{
  "index": 22,
  "text": "Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) obtained from 40 patients who received Hybrid-RT (SABR + LDRT) at the First Affiliated Hospital of University of Science and Technology of China (USTC) were isolated within 2 h of EDTA anticoagulated blood collection using Ficoll-Paque (Cat. #17144002, Cytiva) density gradient centrifugation. All patients completed chemoimmunotherapy \u22652 weeks prior to Hybrid-RT. Peripheral blood was collected immediately before radiotherapy and 3 weeks after treatment completion. Immune cells were analyzed via clinical-grade flow cytometry and were defined as follows: CD3+ T cells (CD45+CD3+), T helper cells (Th; CD45+CD3+CD4+CD8\u2212), granzyme B (GZMB)+ Th cells (CD45+CD3+CD4+CD8\u2212GZMB+), CD8+ T cells (CD45+CD3+CD8+CD4\u2212), cytotoxic CD8+ T cells (cyto-CD8+ T; CD45+CD3+CD8+CD4\u2212GZMB+), natural killer cells (NK; CD45+CD3\u2212CD56dim), and cytotoxic NK cells (cyto-NK; CD45+CD3\u2212CD56dimGZMB+).",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 24,
  "text": "C57BL/6 mice (5 weeks old, male) were obtained from Shanghai SLAC Laboratory Animal Co., Ltd. and housed in a specific pathogen-free barrier facility at the Core Facility Center of the First Affiliated Hospital of USTC. Murine Lewis lung carcinoma (LLC) cells (Cat. #QuiCell-L214, QuiCell Biotechnology Co., Ltd.) were cultured in Dulbecco\u2019s modified Eagle medium (DMEM) supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum (FBS) at 37 \u00b0C with 5% CO\u2082. DMEM (Cat. #10566016, Gibco) and FBS (Cat. #A5669701, Gibco) were purchased from Ketu Biotech Co., Ltd. Mycoplasma contamination was routinely monitored every 2 weeks. Subcutaneous tumors (primary lesions) were established by injecting 2.5 \u00d7 105 LLC cells into the right flank on day \u201321, and lung metastases were induced on the same day by intravenous injection of 5 \u00d7 105 LLC cells via the tail vein (experimental metastasis model). From day \u201321 to day 0, tumors were allowed to grow without intervention.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 25,
  "text": "SABR was delivered on days 1, 3, and 5; LDRT was delivered on days 7, 12, and 17. Anti-programmed death receptor 1 (anti-PD-1; Cat. #BE0146, BioXCell), anti-C-X-C motif chemokine receptor 3 (anti-Cxcr3; Cat. #BE0249, BioXCell), and anti-natural killer group 2 member D (anti-NKG2D; Cat. #BE0111, BioXCell) were administered intraperitoneally at 200 \u03bcg per mouse on days 7, 12, and 17. For irradiation, tumor-bearing mice were anesthetized with isoflurane (induction 2%, maintenance 1.5%; Cat. #HY-A0134, MedChemExpress), and the irradiation sites were fully exposed. Targeted pulmonary or subcutaneous tumors were irradiated using a rodent-specific x-ray irradiator (Cat. #SHARP 100, Raycision Medical Technology Co., Ltd.). For lung metastatic lesions, a dose of 1 Gy (1 Gy/min, 225 kV) was delivered to the entire lung, while subcutaneous tumors (primary lesions) received 8 Gy (1 Gy/min, 225 kV). Serial micro-CT imaging was performed using a micro-CT scanner (Cat. #IMAGING 100, Raycision Medical Technology Co., Ltd.) on days 0, 7, and 21. Tumor volume (V) was calculated as V = (length \u00d7 width2)/2, where length was the longest diameter and width was the perpendicular diameter. Mice were euthanized on day 21, and tumors, lung tissues, and serum were collected for analysis.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 27,
  "text": "Tissue samples were fixed in 4% paraformaldehyde (Cat. #BL539A, Biosharp) for 24 h, paraffin-embedded, and sectioned at 4 \u03bcm thickness. For hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) staining, sections were deparaffinized, rehydrated, and stained according to standard protocols. For Masson\u2019s staining, sections were stained with a Masson\u2019s trichrome stain kit (Cat. #C0189S, Beyotime) according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. For immunohistochemistry (IHC), antigen retrieval was performed using citrate buffer (pH 6.0; Cat. #BL604A, Biosharp) at 95 \u00b0C for 15 min, followed by blocking of endogenous peroxidase activity with 3% hydrogen peroxide (Cat. #abs9333, Absin). Sections were incubated overnight at 4 \u00b0C with primary antibodies against NK1.1 (Cat. #ab289542, Abcam), transforming growth factor-beta (TGF-\u03b2; Cat. #21898-1-AP, Proteintech), followed by incubation with secondary antibodies at 37 \u00b0C for 1 h, and visualized using a 3,3\u2032-diaminobenzidine substrate kit (Cat. #ab64238, Abcam). The antibodies used for IHC staining are listed in Table S3. After hematoxylin counterstaining, staining intensity and distribution were quantified using Fiji software (ImageJ v1.53t, https://fiji.sc/) based on standardized thresholds.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 31,
  "text": "Single-cell suspensions were prepared from lung/tumor tissues by mechanical dissociation and filtration through a 70-\u03bcm filter. The cells were washed in cold phosphate-buffered saline (PBS, Cat. #BL302A, Biosharp), resuspended at 1 \u00d7 107 cells/ml, and Fc-blocked (Cat. #15660, BioLegend) prior to surface staining. To explore intracellular targets, cells were fixed/permeabilized with BD Cytofix/Cytoperm (Cat. #554714, BD Biosciences) and then stained with antibodies against cytokines/activation markers. The samples were analyzed on a BD FACSCelesta using FlowJo (v10.9, https://www.flowjo.com/docs/flowjo10). Details regarding the antibodies used are provided in Table S3.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 33,
  "text": "All tissue samples were collected on day 21. Fresh tissue samples (n = 3/group) were dissociated into single-cell suspensions using the GentleMACS Dissociator (Cat. #130-093-235, Miltenyi Biotec) and filtered through 30-\u03bcm strainers. Cell viability (>85%) was confirmed via Trypan blue (Cat. #T8154, Sigma-Aldrich) exclusion. The fixed cells were hybridized with species-specific probes using the Chromium X system (10x Genomics, Pleasanton). The obtained libraries were sequenced on the NovaSeq 6000 platform (Illumina; 150 bp paired-end, \u226520,000 reads/cell). The data were processed with Cell Ranger (v7.1.0, https://support.10xgenomics.com/) and analyzed using Seurat (v4.3, https://satijalab.org/seurat/), excluding low-quality cells (<500 genes/cell, >15% mitochondrial reads). Gene set enrichment analysis (GSEA) was performed using clusterProfiler (v4.6.0) in R (v4.3.1, https://www.r-project.org/) against MSigDB (https://www.gsea-msigdb.org/gsea/msigdb) hallmark gene sets; pathways with false discovery rate (FDR) < 0.25 were considered significant. The scRNA-seq analysis was performed by OE Biotech (Shanghai, China).",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 37,
  "text": "Serum levels of cytokines were quantified using the Luminex X-200 system (Luminex) according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions (LX-MultiDTH-10, LabEx Co.).",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 39,
  "text": "Clinical efficacy analyses followed the intention-to-treat (ITT) principle. Based on historical control data 26\u201328, a sample size of 74 patients (including an estimated 10% dropout rate) was calculated to provide 80% power to detect an improvement in the 1-year PFS rate from 35% to 50%, using a one-sided \u03b1 level of 0.05. The cutoff date was 2025 September 30. For the clinical trial, survival outcomes were measured from first-line chemoimmunotherapy initiation. The comprehensive clinical statistical analysis plan is provided in the Data S2. SPP1+ macrophage-associated signature scores were calculated using bulk RNA-sequencing data from The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) lung adenocarcinoma (LUAD) and lung squamous cell carcinoma (LUSC) cohorts (https://www.cancer.gov/tcga). Single-sample gene set enrichment analysis (ssGSEA) was performed using a marker gene set derived from the GSE127465 single-cell RNA-sequencing dataset. These scores reflect transcriptional enrichment. The optimal cutoff for the SPP1+ macrophage-associated signature score was determined using the survminer R package (v0.5.1). Patients were classified into high-score (\u2265 cutoff) and low-score (< cutoff) groups. All experiments were independently replicated 3 times with consistent results, and representative data are shown. The statistical tests used for data analysis included Student\u2019s t test, one-way repeated-measures analysis of variance (ANOVA), the \u03c72 test,

{
  "index": 29,
  "text": "Tissues were prepared as described for IHC. Sections were incubated overnight at 4 \u00b0C with primary antibodies against CD8 (Cat. #ab217344, Abcam), CD3 (Cat. #ab135372, Abcam), NK1.1 (Cat. #ab289542, Abcam), CXCR3 (Cat. #ab288437, Abcam), C-X-C motif chemokine ligand 10 (CXCL10, Cat. #10937-1-AP, Proteintech), GZMB (Cat. #13588-1-AP, Proteintech), F4/80 (Cat. #sc-52664, Santa Cruz), and secreted phosphoprotein 1 (SPP1, Cat. #sc-21742, Santa Cruz). After washing, sections were incubated at room temperature for 1 h with Cy3 Goat-Anti-Rabbit IgG (H + L) (Cat. #ab6939, Abcam), Alexa Fluor 488 Goat-Anti-Mouse IgG (H + L) (Cat. #ab150113, Abcam), and Cy5 Goat-Anti-Rabbit IgG (H + L) (Cat. #ab6564, Abcam). The antibodies used for multiplex immunofluorescence (mIF) staining are listed in Table S3. Sections were mounted with 4\u2032,6-diamidino-2-phenylindole (DAPI) containing anti-fade mounting medium (Cat. #F6057, Sigma) and examined by fluorescence microscopy.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 35,
  "text": "Cell\u2013cell communication networks were inferred using CellChat (v2.1.2) in R (v4.3.1, https://www.r-project.org/). The normalized expression matrix was imported and used to generate a CellChat object, followed by preprocessing to identify overexpressed genes and ligand\u2013receptor interactions using default parameters. Communication probabilities were calculated (computeCommunProb) and filtered to exclude interactions with fewer than 10 cells (filterCommunication), and pathway-level networks were aggregated (aggregateNet). Signaling pathways were prioritized on the basis of interaction strength and network centrality.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

{
  "index": 11,
  "text": "This single-arm, multicenter, prospective phase II clinical study was conducted at 4 medical centers across China. The clinical trial was registered at ClinicalTrials.gov under the identifier NCT05348668. Eligible participants (18 to 75 years) had histologically confirmed stage IV driver-negative NSCLC (8th edition of the Tumor\u2013Node\u2013Metastasis [TNM] Staging System 24), Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status 0 to 1, and adequate organ/bone marrow function. Exclusion criteria included driver mutations (e.g., epidermal growth factor receptor [EGFR], anaplastic lymphoma kinase [ALK], and ROS proto-oncogene 1 [ROS1]), pulmonary fibrosis, autoimmune disease, active infection, or serious comorbidities. All patients received 4 to 6 cycles of platinum-based doublet chemotherapy plus ICI. Patients without disease progression after comprehensive evaluation subsequently underwent Hybrid-RT during ICI maintenance. The comprehensive clinical trial protocol is provided in Data S1.",
  "style": "Normal",
  "is_heading": false
}

